00:02:39.271 --> 00:02:40.987
- [Voiceover] Dimitri asks,

00:02:40.987 --> 00:02:43.933
"How do you prepare for
an important keynote?"

00:02:45.975 --> 00:02:49.507
- Dimitri, the way I
prepare for a keynote is to

00:02:49.507 --> 00:02:52.223
think about punching every audience member

00:02:52.223 --> 00:02:53.962
directly in the mouth.

00:02:53.962 --> 00:02:57.629
I look at the audience as
my enemy, yet my child.

00:02:58.074 --> 00:03:00.510
There's this kind of weird mix between

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:02.510
loving them with all my heart

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:05.410
and really wanting them
to get the message.

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:08.058
There's a disrespect and there's a love,

00:03:08.058 --> 00:03:09.938
and that mix is what I do.

00:03:09.938 --> 00:03:13.306
I'm literally like a boxer
before hitting the ring

00:03:13.306 --> 00:03:14.886
six minutes before I take stage.

00:03:14.886 --> 00:03:16.578
Maybe that's where Jab Jab
Jab Right Hook came from

00:03:16.578 --> 00:03:19.274
in some ways, because I'm
literally in this crazy zone.

00:03:19.274 --> 00:03:20.897
Eight minutes before I'm talking,

00:03:20.897 --> 00:03:22.942
I don't even know that I'm giving a talk.

00:03:22.942 --> 00:03:24.913
I'm like just like doing
my email, I'm just like

00:03:24.913 --> 00:03:26.842
laughing, crying about the Jets,

00:03:26.842 --> 00:03:29.373
like you know whatever it is,
but around six minute zone,

00:03:29.373 --> 00:03:33.346
I go into this weird place
and I get very focused and

00:03:33.346 --> 00:03:36.843
I say to myself, "You're only
as good as your last talk."

00:03:36.843 --> 00:03:38.941
And so even though I've
had a great seven year

00:03:38.941 --> 00:03:42.073
public speaking career,
none of that matters

00:03:42.073 --> 00:03:44.605
the second I take that
stage for the next time,

00:03:44.605 --> 00:03:46.972
because you're only as
good as your last at bat.

00:03:46.972 --> 00:03:49.553
And so, my friend, to answer
your question, Dimitri,

00:03:49.553 --> 00:03:52.776
the way I prepare for
a speaking engagement

00:03:52.776 --> 00:03:56.278
is the same way I would prepare for war.

